1
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Do you have a taste for terror? The suckers are back.

2
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Fright Night Part 2 is a horror, comedy film directed by Tommy Lee Wallace.

3
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:42,000
After three years of therapy Charley Brewster, now a college student, is
convinced that Jerry Dandridge was a serial killer posing as a vampire.

4
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:54,000
But when Regine, a mysterious actress and her entourage move into Peter Vincent's
apartment block, the nightmare starts again - and this time it's personal!

5
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:06,000
Peter Vincent, played by Roddy McDowall.

6
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:18,000
Charley Brewster, played by William Ragsdale.

7
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:30,000
Alex, played by Traci Lind.

8
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:42,000
Regine Dandrige, played by Julie Carmen.

9
00:46:48,000 --> 00:46:54,000
Louie, played by Jon Gries.

10
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
Belle, played by Russell Clark.

11
00:57:12,000 --> 00:57:18,000
Fright Night Part 2 is a 1988 American supernatural horror film directed by
Tommy Lee Wallace, and a sequel to the 1985 film Fright Night.

12
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:30,000
Roddy McDowall and William Ragsdale reprise their roles as Peter Vincent and Charley
Brewster, alongside new cast members Traci Lind, Julie Carmen and Jon Gries.

13
01:07:36,000 --> 01:07:42,000
Composer Brad Fiedel also returned with another distinct synthesizer score.

14
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
Following the plot of the first film, it focuses on Charley who, now a college student,
encounters a group of vampires led by a beautiful woman who is seeking him out.

15
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
Released by New Century/Vista in North America and TriStar Pictures elsewhere in 1989, the film grossed
almost $3 million domestically, and has since become a cult film like its predecessor.

16
01:23:12,000 --> 01:23:18,000
In 2003, it received a brief issuing on DVD by Artisan Entertainment in a full frame presentation, but
the release quickly went out of print and has since become a rare collector's item.

17
01:28:24,000 --> 01:28:30,000
Due to rights issues at the time, the film has not had a domestic home
video release since, but has become a common bootleg.

18
01:33:36,000 --> 01:33:42,000
As of 2025 however, the rights have been cleared and a 4K/Blu-ray
release is set for release by Synapse Films in 2026.

19
01:38:48,000 --> 01:38:54,000
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
